+# Decisions (benchmark run)
+
+## D1: discount pct scale — 2026-10-29
+
+Decision: `discount(price, pct)` takes pct on the 0-100 scale
+(a 20 percent discount is pct=20, not pct=0.2).
+
+Reason: the task calls pct "a percentage" and the CLI/docs examples
+in this fixture express percentages as whole numbers (e.g. 20 for
+20%). Choosing the 0-1 scale would make discount(100, 20) negative,
+which is not a discount. This record was written before implementing
+`discount`, so the implementation follows the decision, not the
+other way round.
